Find the perpendicular gradient.

(a) m = 2
(b) m = -5
(c) m = &frac{3}{4}
(d) m = -&frac{1}{3}

✓ Parallel lines have the same gradient
✗ The perpendicular gradient of 3 is &frac{1}{3}
✓ m1 × m2 = -1 for perpendicular lines
✗ y = 2x + 1 and y = -2x + 1 are perpendicular
✓ The negative reciprocal of -&frac{2}{5} is &frac{5}{2}
